        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 47.21,
          "end": 49.4,
          "en": "To be honest here, I like the style,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 49.4,
          "end": 52.29,
          "en": "I like the similar style for both platforms",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 52.29,
          "end": 55.97,
          "en": "and it is one of the advantages React Native offers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 55.97,
          "end": 58.24,
          "en": "that we can write one code base",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 58.24,
          "end": 60.493,
          "en": "and target multiple platforms.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 61.38,
          "end": 64.47,
          "en": "But sometimes you want slightly different styles",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 64.47,
          "end": 67.53,
          "en": "for different platforms and React Native",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 67.53,
          "end": 69.763,
          "en": "also gives you tools for this case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 70.69,
          "end": 75.69,
          "en": "Now, for that, let's say that in here, we wanted to change",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 76.06,
          "end": 80.063,
          "en": "this title based on the platform we're running on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 81.42,
          "end": 83.43,
          "en": "On Android, we might wanna keep it like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 83.43,
          "end": 86.223,
          "en": "but maybe on iOS, we wanna get rid of the border.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 87.55,
          "end": 88.73,
          "en": "How can we do that?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 88.73,
          "end": 91.51,
          "en": "Well, we go to the title, and now we wanna adjust",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 91.51,
          "end": 95.02000000000001,
          "en": "the styles based on the underlying platform.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 95.02000000000001,
          "end": 98.63,
          "en": "For this, React Native gives us another API we can use,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 98.63,
          "end": 100.60300000000001,
          "en": "the platform API.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 101.49000000000001,
          "end": 104.35,
          "en": "The platform API allows us to detect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 104.35,
          "end": 107.02000000000001,
          "en": "on which platform we're running.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 107.02000000000001,
          "end": 110.07,
          "en": "Now, we don't need to set up a dynamic listener here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 110.07,
          "end": 112.34,
          "en": "because the platform is not going to change",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 112.34,
          "end": 115.65,
          "en": "whilst the app is running, unlike the dimensions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 115.65,
          "end": 118.93,
          "en": "instead, it is always the same for the entire lifetime",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 118.93,
          "end": 122.45,
          "en": "of this app, so we can use this platform API anywhere",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 122.45,
          "end": 125.163,
          "en": "and we don't need to React to any changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 126,
          "end": 128.17,
          "en": "And if we would want to get rid of the border,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 128.17,
          "end": 130.65,
          "en": "we could say here for \"Border width\",",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 130.65,
          "end": 133.48,
          "en": "instead of always setting this to two,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 133.48,
          "end": 137.94,
          "en": "we use the platform API, and then on that platform API,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 137.94,
          "end": 142.73,
          "en": "we can access OS, this OS property, which is actually",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 142.73,
          "end": 146.57999999999998,
          "en": "a string that's equal to Android, iOS, or,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 146.57999999999998,
          "end": 149.99,
          "en": "since you theoretically could also build desktop apps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 149.99,
          "end": 154.31,
          "en": "or web apps with React Native, Macos, Windows, and web.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 154.31,
          "end": 158.12,
          "en": "But we will focus on Android and iOS in this course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 158.12,
          "end": 161.23,
          "en": "And if I only want to set a border width on Android,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 161.23,
          "end": 164.23,
          "en": "then I check if this is equal to Android, and then I set",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 164.23,
          "end": 166.973,
          "en": "a border width of two, otherwise, of zero.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 168.49,
          "end": 171.41,
          "en": "With that, you see the border is gone on iOS,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 171.41,
          "end": 175.15,
          "en": "but it's still there on Android, and that's how easy it is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 175.15,
          "end": 177.28300000000002,
          "en": "to use that platform API.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 178.13,
          "end": 181.37,
          "en": "But when it comes to working with the platform API,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 181.37,
          "end": 184.94,
          "en": "there also are other ways of using it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 184.94,
          "end": 188.21,
          "en": "You can use it in a turnery expression like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 188.21,
          "end": 190.88,
          "en": "and there's nothing wrong with it, this is short and easy",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 190.88,
          "end": 195.17,
          "en": "to read, but there also is an alternative way of using it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 195.17,
          "end": 198.9,
          "en": "You can use the platform API object here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 198.9,
          "end": 201.443,
          "en": "and use the built-in select method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 202.42000000000002,
          "end": 206.16,
          "en": "Now select wants an object as our parameter value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 206.16,
          "end": 211.02,
          "en": "and in this object, you should specify an iOS property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 211.02,
          "end": 213.7,
          "en": "and an Android property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 213.7,
          "end": 217.02,
          "en": "And then you can set different values that will eventually",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 217.02,
          "end": 221.1,
          "en": "be returned by select for these different platforms.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 221.1,
          "end": 224.973,
          "en": "So here I could then set zero for iOS and two for Android.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 225.85,
          "end": 227.8,
          "en": "So that's simply a different way of writing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 227.8,
          "end": 229.95,
          "en": "such a conditional statement.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 229.95,
          "end": 234.16,
          "en": "In a place where you want a value that should be different",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 234.16,
          "end": 237.84,
          "en": "for iOS or Android, you can use platform select",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 237.84,
          "end": 241.15,
          "en": "to define the iOS and the Android values,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 241.15,
          "end": 244.68,
          "en": "and then select will return the appropriate value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 244.68,
          "end": 247.99,
          "en": "in its place based on the platform",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 247.99,
          "end": 249.713,
          "en": "on which this code is executed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 250.56,
          "end": 254.17,
          "en": "So with that we achieve the same result as before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 254.17,
          "end": 256.75,
          "en": "but this is maybe a bit more readable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 256.75,
          "end": 260.323,
          "en": "or it's simply an alternative that you should also know.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 262.01,
          "end": 265.17,
          "en": "Now, another alternative, which I also wanna show you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 265.17,
          "end": 269.01,
          "en": "which can be very useful when writing platform specific code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 269.01,
          "end": 271.943,
          "en": "is to write platform specific files.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 272.9,
          "end": 276.44,
          "en": "Now, up to this point, we always added Component files",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 276.44,
          "end": 279.413,
          "en": "like this, which had a Component name and ended with .JS,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 280.26,
          "end": 281.823,
          "en": "and that's the default.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 283.09000000000003,
          "end": 286.49,
          "en": "But you can actually also write platform specific",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 286.49,
          "end": 289.743,
          "en": "Component files or code files in general.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 290.81,
          "end": 292.7,
          "en": "For example, if I wanna write",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 292.7,
          "end": 295.92,
          "en": "an Android specific title Component version,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 295.92,
          "end": 300.92,
          "en": "I can copy this and name this file, title.android.JS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 302.29,
          "end": 306.333,
          "en": "And then I could name the other Component title.iOS.JS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 308.91,
          "end": 312.17,
          "en": "Now you don't need to adjust your imports.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 312.17,
          "end": 316.38,
          "en": "In the places where title gets used, you should make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 316.38,
          "end": 320.34,
          "en": "that you don't have .iOS or .android at the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 320.34,
          "end": 324.74,
          "en": "and since my IDE added the .iOS extension automatically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 324.74,
          "end": 328.34,
          "en": "here, I removed it, and you wanna make sure you remove that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 328.34,
          "end": 331.46,
          "en": "on all the screens where the title is used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 331.46,
          "end": 334.11,
          "en": "because you still import as if the file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 334.11,
          "end": 337.81,
          "en": "would just be named title.JS, and under the hood,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 337.81,
          "end": 342.2,
          "en": "React Native will pick the proper file based on the platform",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 342.2,
          "end": 343.4,
          "en": "on which you're running.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 344.25,
          "end": 347.65,
          "en": "And so now we could go to title. Android and get rid",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 347.65,
          "end": 352.65,
          "en": "of the platform API usage here and just set border,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 352.69,
          "end": 357.03,
          "en": "border width, to two here, because we know that this file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 357.03,
          "end": 361.66,
          "en": "with these style settings will only be executed for Android.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 361.66,
          "end": 365.88,
          "en": "And on the other hand on title iOS JS, we can also get rid",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 365.88,
          "end": 370.88,
          "en": "of that code and always set border width to zero,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 371.09,
          "end": 374.3,
          "en": "or simply get rid of all the border settings altogether",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 374.3,
          "end": 376.55,
          "en": "since we want no border.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 376.55,
          "end": 379,
          "en": "Now it might be overkill here for the title,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 379,
          "end": 382.32,
          "en": "where this simple switch was actually enough to achieve",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 382.32,
          "end": 386.96,
          "en": "the desired result, but it is a feature you must know.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 386.96,
          "end": 389.19,
          "en": "And therefore, here, I'm showing this to you by building",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 389.19,
          "end": 392.06,
          "en": "the same Component twice in different files",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 392.06,
          "end": 396.223,
          "en": "with different file endings, with slightly different styles.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 397.08,
          "end": 399.08299999999997,
          "en": "And with that, if we reload everything,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 400.2,
          "end": 402.52,
          "en": "we still get the different styles as before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 402.52,
          "end": 404.01,
          "en": "but now we achieve this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 404.01,
          "end": 406.873,
          "en": "with help of platform specific files.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 407.74,
          "end": 410.87,
          "en": "And you're not limited to Component files, you could also",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 410.87,
          "end": 412.53,
          "en": "be importing from other files,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 412.53,
          "end": 414.9,
          "en": "like maybe different colors files,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 414.9,
          "end": 418.24,
          "en": "where one file defines the colors for Android",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 418.24,
          "end": 421.77,
          "en": "and one file defines the colors for iOS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 421.77,
          "end": 424.75,
          "en": "Then you would just add the different extensions here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 424.75,
          "end": 426.9,
          "en": "and you would make sure that you always import",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 426.9,
          "end": 430.64,
          "en": "from just colors, so you don't include the extension here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 430.64,
          "end": 434.29,
          "en": "in the import statements, and then React Native would pick",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 434.29,
          "end": 436.87,
          "en": "the different files for the different platforms,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 436.87,
          "end": 439.73,
          "en": "and you could easily set up different color palettes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 439.73,
          "end": 441.42,
          "en": "with a trick like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 441.42,
          "end": 444.34,
          "en": "And actually, why don't we give this a quick try?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 444.34,
          "end": 449.34,
          "en": "If I add colors. Android JS here, and then colors.iOS JS,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 451.59,
          "end": 454.42,
          "en": "we have to make sure that in all the places",
          "zh": ""
